  <!-- EN: questDescription(installation==DMS_VaultStationSite)-&gt;A supply manifest recovered from remnant traffic lists a [siteFactionName] storage vault, and the surface station that sits on top of it. The station is still manned by (*Threat)[enemiesCount] [enemiesLabel](/Threat), and heavy units are among them.\n\nThe freight elevator into the vault is locked under an armored cover plate, slaved to the access console beside it. The console takes a key-card, not a hack: swipe one and the plate retracts. The car still has power, so what is below was never collected.\n\nThe manifest&apos;s location fix expires in [siteTimeout]. After that the station will relocate and its position will be lost.\n\nThe installation also runs a site server: a small records host that can be hacked once for blueprints or access keys, at the cost of setting off the alarm.\n\nCaution: it is a hostile installation. Once you enter, its monitoring protocol will summon enemy reinforcements after a countdown. Get the shaft open, then decide whether to hold the surface or go down. -->
  <!-- EN: questDescription(installation==DMS_RepairStationSite)-&gt;A maintenance request on the remnant network leads to a [siteFactionName] field repair depot. The depot is guarded by (*Threat)[enemiesCount] [enemiesLabel](/Threat): engineers, riflemen and a drone screen.\n\nTwo units are still clamped in the depot&apos;s cradles, in hibernation, behind a sealed maintenance door. They were never re-authenticated after servicing, so a mechanitor with spare bandwidth can hack one and take it. The depot&apos;s security console releases the door. There is also a mobile crew lifter on the pad and a stock of tungsteel in the stores.\n\nThe request&apos;s location fix expires in [siteTimeout]. After that the depot will relocate and its position will be lost.\n\nThe installation also runs a site server: a small records host that can be hacked once for blueprints or access keys, at the cost of setting off the alarm.\n\nCaution: it is a hostile installation. Once you enter, its monitoring protocol will summon enemy reinforcements after a countdown. -->
  <!-- EN: questDescription(installation==DMS_OperationBaseSite)-&gt;Remnant traffic has given away a [siteFactionName] forward operating base. It is held by (*Threat)[enemiesCount] [enemiesLabel](/Threat): line infantry behind the wire, with heavy support and night-capable units in reserve.\n\nThe base is a supply hub. Crates of rations, small arms, spare parts and prosthetics sit in the open, and a freight elevator at the back of the compound leads down into a buried store. The blast doors in front of it answer to two security consoles; hack both to open the way, then hack the lift itself.\n\nThe position fix holds for [siteTimeout]. After that the base will strike camp and its position will be lost.\n\nThe installation also runs a site server: a small records host that can be hacked once for blueprints or access keys, at the cost of setting off the alarm.\n\nCaution: it is a hostile installation. Once you enter, its monitoring protocol will summon enemy reinforcements after a countdown. -->
  <!-- EN: questDescription(installation==DMS_SiteStationSite)-&gt;A pre-war station, half of it collapsed, has been located nearby. A [siteFactionName] detachment has dug into the ruins: (*Threat)[enemiesCount] [enemiesLabel](/Threat), shield-bearers and infantry with drone and lifter support, spread across the station&apos;s halls.\n\nThe station was abandoned in a hurry. Ancient supply crates, industrial shelving and the wrecks of the old security systems are still scattered through it, along with a working pod launcher pair. Everything the detachment has not already stripped is yours.\n\nThe detachment is expected to move on in [siteTimeout]. After that the station will be picked clean and no longer worth the trip.\n\nThe installation also runs a site server: a small records host that can be hacked once for blueprints or access keys, at the cost of setting off the alarm.\n\nOne of the station&apos;s freight elevators still runs down to a data archive the fleet buried beneath it. A facility server core sits in the sealed server hall at the bottom; it can be hacked several times, and every attempt will bring the archive&apos;s defences up from below. The corridors are fitted with gas vents, and a lockdown controller will seal the lift a minute after the alert level maxes out.\n\nCaution: it is a hostile installation. Once you enter, its monitoring protocol will summon enemy reinforcements after a countdown, and the station is large enough to get lost in. -->
  <!-- EN: questDescription(installation==DMS_LaunchSiteSite)-&gt;An old missile launch complex has turned up on the scanners. The launchers were destroyed long ago and the compound is falling apart, but a [siteFactionName] patrol of (*Threat)[enemiesCount] [enemiesLabel](/Threat) still sweeps the wreckage.\n\nNobody ever salvaged the place. Wrecked automatroids, a logistics container, sensor and radar mounts and the remains of the launch crews&apos; equipment are all still where they fell.\n\nThe patrol&apos;s schedule puts it there for another [siteTimeout]. After that it moves on and the site&apos;s position is lost.\n\nThe installation also runs a site server: a small records host that can be hacked once for blueprints or access keys, at the cost of setting off the alarm.\n\nCaution: it is a hostile installation. Once you enter, the patrol&apos;s monitoring protocol will summon enemy reinforcements after a countdown. -->
